  "publicacion": {
    "titulo": "She washed clothes for 75 years, then gave a university $150,000",
    "descripcion": "Oseola McCarty left school in the sixth grade and spent three-quarters of a century washing and ironing other people's clothes in Hattiesburg, Mississippi. She never owned a car and had a TV with one local channel. In 1995 she gave $150,000, more than half of her $280,000 estate, to the University of Southern Mississippi, a campus blocks from her house that she had never visited. By 2014 the scholarship fund topped $700,000 and 44 students had received McCarty Scholarships. Her story is rare: saving like that cost her decades of comfort. Not financial advice.\n\nSource: Mississippi Encyclopedia, https://mississippiencyclopedia.org/entries/oseola-mccarty/",
